	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["44EA00000000000E"]
			description: [
				"&6&lThe Steam Age.&r"
				""
				"First SU taught you the loop: make rotation, spend it carefully, build a Precision Mechanism. This chapter is what that rotation is actually &ofor&r."
				""
				"&6&lThree things happen here, and they are worth knowing apart:&r"
				""
				"&e1. Logistics.&r Belts, funnels, chutes and vaults - moving items between machines without a hopper in sight. This is the half of Create most packs never explain, and it is the half that replaces early pipes."
				""
				"&e2. Contraptions.&r Bearings, chassis and super glue let you pick a structure up and &omove&r it - drills that dig, harvesters that farm, and doors that are honestly just showing off."
				""
				"&e3. Steam.&r Water wheels cap out fast. Steam Engines burn fuel to make far more SU from one block, and they are what carries you from a hand-built workshop to something that runs while you are on another planet."
				""
				"&7Nothing in here is required to finish the pack - but Create automation is the cheapest automation in the game, and it works long before you can afford an ME system.&r"
			]
			icon: "create:steam_engine"
			id: "7F00000000000000"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7F00000000000100"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7What all that rotation is for"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7F00000000000200"
				title: "Begin the Steam Age"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&eThe Steam Age"
