		{
			dependencies: ["7F00000000000001"]
			description: [
				"A &eClutch&r cuts rotation when powered. A &eGearshift&r reverses it."
				""
				"&e&lThese are your on/off switch and your reverse gear.&r Without them, a Create build runs the moment it has torque and never stops."
				""
				"&7Clutch: redstone on = downstream stops. Gearshift: redstone on = downstream spins the other way.&r"
				""
				"&e&lThe classic use is a piston contraption&r that needs to go out and come back - gearshift on the return, triggered by an observer or a timer."
				""
				"&8Pair with the Sequenced Gearshift below when you need timed, repeatable motion rather than a simple toggle."
			]
			icon: "create:clutch"
			id: "7F00000000000002"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7F01000000000002"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Redstone control of rotation"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7F02000000000200"
					item: "create:clutch"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7F02000000000201"
					item: "create:gearshift"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&eClutch & Gearshift"
			x: -12.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7F00000000000002"]
			description: [
				"The &eSequenced Gearshift&r runs a short program of rotation: turn this many degrees, wait, reverse, repeat."
				""
				"&e&lThis is how contraptions do precise, repeatable movement.&r A door that opens exactly 90 degrees, a drill that extends five blocks and retracts, a bridge that unfolds."
				""
				"&7Right-click to open the instruction list. Each row is one step - turn by angle, turn by distance, wait, or await a redstone signal. It runs the list once per redstone pulse.&r"
				""
				"&8The single most useful Create block for anyone who wants machines that look alive rather than just spinning."
			]
			icon: "create:sequenced_gearshift"
			id: "7F00000000000003"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7F01000000000003"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Programmed motion"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7F02000000000300"
				item: "create:sequenced_gearshift"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&eSequenced Gearshift"
			x: -12.0d
			y: -4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7F00000000000002"]
			description: [
				"The &eRotation Speed Controller&r sets the speed of a Large Cogwheel above it to any value you choose, regardless of input speed."
				""
				"&e&lThis removes the whole gearing puzzle.&r Instead of chaining cogwheels to reach a speed, you dial it in - including negative values to reverse."
				""
				"&c&lIt is expensive in stress.&r Speeding rotation up costs stress proportionally, so a controller cranked to maximum on a big network will brown out everything else."
				""
				"&7The correct use is one machine that needs a specific speed - a Mechanical Saw that wants to be slow, or a Millstone you want fast - rather than as the backbone of the whole build.&r"
			]
			icon: "create:rotation_speed_controller"
			id: "7F00000000000004"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7F01000000000004"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Set an exact RPM"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7F02000000000400"
				item: "create:rotation_speed_controller"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&eRotation Speed Controller"
			x: -10.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7F00000000000004"]
			description: [
				"A &eHand Crank&r gives you a burst of rotation on demand. A &eWindmill Bearing&r plus sails gives you free rotation forever."
				""
				"&e&lWindmills are the skyblock answer.&r Build a bearing, attach a cross of sail blocks, glue it together and start it. More sails means more stress capacity, and unlike a water wheel it needs no water and no fall."
				""
				"&7You need at least eight sail blocks for it to start. Bigger windmills are dramatically stronger - and on a floating island there is nothing to obstruct one.&r"
				""
				"&8Hand cranks are for one-off jobs: a single deployer, a door, a mechanical crafter you use twice. Do not build a base around one."
			]
			icon: "create:hand_crank"
			id: "7F00000000000005"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7F01000000000005"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Power without a water wheel"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7F02000000000500"
