		{
			dependencies: ["7F00000000000006"]
			description: [
				"&eFunnels&r move items between belts, chests and machines - the connective tissue of every Create build."
				""
				"&e&lAndesite versus Brass:&r andesite funnels move items and nothing more. &7Brass funnels take a filter&r, so they only move what you tell them to."
				""
				"&c&lDirection matters and is easy to get backwards.&r Right-click a funnel with a wrench to flip whether it is inserting or extracting. A funnel facing the wrong way looks identical to a broken one."
				""
				"&7Funnels on a belt pull items off it; funnels on a chest push items onto it. Same block, opposite jobs, decided by which side you attached it to.&r"
			]
			icon: "create:andesite_funnel"
			id: "7F00000000000007"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7F01000000000007"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7In and out of everything"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7F02000000000700"
					item: "create:andesite_funnel"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7F02000000000701"
					item: "create:brass_funnel"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&eFunnels"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7F00000000000007"]
			description: [
				"&eChutes&r move items vertically - the thing belts cannot do."
				""
				"&e&lThey work both ways.&r Items fall down a chute by gravity, or an Encased Fan blowing upward through one will lift them. That is how you get output from a machine on the floor to a chest on the ceiling."
				""
				"&e&lSmart Chutes take a filter&r, exactly like brass funnels, so you can sort vertically."
				""
				"&7Chutes also pick items up off the ground beneath them, which makes them the neatest way to collect drops from a Mechanical Saw or a block breaker.&r"
			]
			icon: "create:chute"
			id: "7F00000000000008"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7F01000000000008"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Vertical item movement"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "7F02000000000800"
					item: "create:chute"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7F02000000000801"
					item: "create:smart_chute"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&eChutes"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7F00000000000008"]
			description: [
				"The &eWeighted Ejector&r flings items to a target you select with a wrench - across a gap, up a level, into a machine."
				""
				"&e&lIt is the cheapest way to cross a gap&r that a belt cannot span, and it looks considerably better than a chute-and-funnel chain."
				""
				"&7Set the target by wrenching the ejector then clicking the destination block. It shows you the arc before you commit.&r"
				""
				"&e&lIt also has a stack-size threshold&r - hold items until N have accumulated, then throw them all at once. Useful for batching."
			]
			icon: "create:weighted_ejector"
			id: "7F00000000000009"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7F01000000000009"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Launch items where you want them"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7F02000000000900"
