		{
			dependencies: ["6187A9055B14303B"]
			description: [
				"A &eTrack Station&r is where trains are assembled and dispatched; a &eSchedule&r is the program that tells one where to go."
				""
				"&e&lThe schedule is the actual feature.&r Go to station A, wait until cargo is full, go to station B, unload, wait 30 seconds, repeat - handed to a Conductor, the train runs that loop forever with nobody aboard."
				""
				"&7Name your stations clearly. Schedules reference them by name, and debugging a train that will not move is usually a typo.&r"
				""
				"&8On a floating island, trains between platforms are genuinely practical - too far to belt, too close to justify an ME network."
			]
			icon: "create:track_station"
			id: "7F0000000000001D"
			rewards: [{
